# Build artifacts
**/node_modules/
**/target/
**/_build/
**/deps/
**/obj/
**/bin/
**/build/
**/.gradle/
**/.venv/
**/vendor/
**/.bundle/
# Cargo.lock is NOT a build artifact for these binary crates -- it is meant
# to be committed like every other lock file here (uv.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml,
# go.sum, composer.lock, Gemfile.lock). This entry used to say otherwise,
# which is almost certainly why 5 of 10 rust-* projects had no committed
# Cargo.lock (a review found them, then a review found 2 more) with no
# signal: `cargo generate-lockfile` produced a file `git add -A` would
# silently skip. `cargo check --locked` now fails loudly instead -- see
# check-generated-syntax.sh's Rust check and its "no committed Cargo.lock"
# guard.
